      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Two cases are described of intraluminal coronary artery filling defects resembling thrombus caused by nonopacified collateral blood flow mixing with injected contrast just distal to a severe coronary artery stenosis. The term pseudothrombus is ascribed to this appearance to emphasize this differential diagnosis of intraluminal filling defects."},
